WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:06.549
Speaker 1: Speaking of Joe Biden, Joe Biden
has again made the correct decision when it

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:13.270
comes to yet another request from former President
Donald Trump to shield the White House visitor

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:18.880
logs from the days right around the Jan. six,
2021, Trump riots.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.520
Trump wants those to be hidden.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.619
Joe Biden has said no.

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:29.140
Reuters report Biden gives the January 6th
panel access to Trump's White House visitor

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.160
logs.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.510
President Joe Biden has rejected former President
Donald Trump's executive privilege claims

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.910
and ordered White House visitor logs to be
released to the panel investigating the deadly

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:45.740
Jan. six, 2021 attack, according to a letter
released on Wednesday.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.400
In a letter to the National Archives, Biden's
White House counsel granted congressional

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.140
investigators access to the data given the
urgency of their work, probing Trump supporters

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:00.989
violent siege of the Capitol and ordered the
agency to turn over the logs within 15 days,

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.510
15 days.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:06.820
The president has determined meaning Joe Biden,
the president, has determined that an assertion

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:12.070
of executive privilege is not in the best
interests of the United States and therefore

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:16.180
is not justified as to these records and portions
of records.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.960
That's Biden's council counsel, Dana Remus.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:26.320
Importantly, Biden last year also rejected
Trump's bid to block the U.S. House of Representatives

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.340
committee Jan. six committee from accessing
batches of documents from the former president's

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.689
time at the White House.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:38.640
The Associated Press similarly reporting Biden
orders release of Trump White House logs to

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.740
Congress.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.600
The committee has sought a trove of data from
the National Archives, including presidential

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.909
records that Trump fought to keep private.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:50.370
The records being released to Congress or
visitor logs showing appointment information

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:55.030
for individuals allowed to enter the White
House on the day of the insurrection.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.970
Now I have a couple thoughts on this.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:02.140
First of all, as I've said before, just think
about it, you just apply.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:07.920
Your own sense of reason to this is this is
the behavior of someone with nothing to hide.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.149
And the answer is, of course, no.

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:12.400
Of course no.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.769
The second part of this is, you know, who
visits the White House, who visits a presidents

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:22.530
at the president at the White House is just
like base level public information.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:27.760
And so aside from whether, generally speaking,
this is the behavior of someone with nothing

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.579
to hide or of someone with a guilty conscience.

00:02:30.579 --> 00:02:35.999
This is like basic level information that
when you promise to have the most transparent

00:02:35.999 --> 00:02:40.599
administration in history, as Donald Trump
did, Trump ran on.

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:42.420
Obama has not been transparent.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.620
I will be transparent.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.299
And then you try to shield just White House
visitor logs.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:50.639
This is a basic element of transparency.

00:02:50.639 --> 00:02:56.799
But there's another issue which is I would
make a bet that there are many visitors to

00:02:56.799 --> 00:03:01.529
the White House whose names were never put
into the logs in the first place.

00:03:01.529 --> 00:03:07.700
It would be shocking to me if the White House
logs that they are trying to shield are even

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:13.849
complete in terms of representing everybody
that visited Donald Trump at the White House.

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:17.769
And then again, remember last week we learned
about Trump Tower flushing documents and clogging

00:03:17.769 --> 00:03:20.059
the toilet.

00:03:20.059 --> 00:03:24.040
How do we know that there aren't some of these
that have been flushed or attempted to be

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.749
flushed and then fished out of the toilet
by Trump's staff?

00:03:28.749 --> 00:03:29.949
None of it makes sense.

00:03:29.949 --> 00:03:34.059
And if you think back to 2016, you'll remember
Donald Trump saying about Hillary Clinton.

00:03:34.059 --> 00:03:39.129
People who have nothing to hide don't destroy
evidence to keep it from being publicly archived

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:41.400
as required under federal law.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.049
That's what Trump said about Hillary.

00:03:43.049 --> 00:03:48.139
He said Hillary's behavior with documents
is disqualifying to her as president.

00:03:48.139 --> 00:03:55.310
Look at what Trump has done, ripping up documents,
incinerating documents, flushing documents,

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:58.189
begging Joe Biden to hide documents.

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.939
But he said Hillary is the one that we can't
trust.

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:02.680
Of course, it doesn't make any sense.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:08.309
So this is about the release of documents
to the January 6th Committee, not to the public,

00:04:08.309 --> 00:04:13.449
whether those documents will be made public
by being leaked or who knows if and when they

00:04:13.449 --> 00:04:15.169
are given to the Jan. six committee.

00:04:15.169 --> 00:04:21.190
We just don't know yet, but this is the correct
decision and this is further.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.830
A further indication that this is a guy with
a guilty conscience who doesn't want us to

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:33.229
know who visited the White House on that day,
now what might be if, if the logs are complete?

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:36.860
What might they reveal, they might reveal
